{"step_index":532,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T01:44:07Z","input_tokens":7387,"cache_read_tokens":177614,"output_tokens":2581,"thinking":"The user wants the full 77 rows, but only with the 6th column (business registration number) populated. The phrase \"only find the business registration number\" indicates a desire for conciseness, avoiding extraneous information.\n\n\nBegin by compiling the known business registration numbers into a list. The request necessitates verifying the remaining 68 companies to ensure no other registration numbers were missed during the initial sweep. Focus specifically on the list provided as a secondary check for completeness.\n\n\nConfirmed registration numbers from the provided list, preparing the list for cross-referencing against the larger data set to ensure comprehensive retrieval of all 77 entries and populate the target column. The presence of duplicate numbers suggests a potential need for de-duplication depending on the final expected output format.\n\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"const fs = require('fs');\n\nconst targets = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('target_companies.json', 'utf8'));\n\nfunction cleanName(n) {\n  return n.replace(/\\(주\\)|\\(유한\\)|\\(유책\\)|\\(합자\\)|\\(사\\)/g, '').replace(/주식회사|유한회사/g, '').trim();\n}\n\nasync function searchMarketbz(cleanQuery) {\n  try {\n    const url = `https://marketbz.com/업체명으로기업조회/${encodeURIComponent(cleanQuery)}`;\n    const res = await fetch(url, { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0' } });\n    if (!res.ok) return [];\n    const text = await res.text();\n    const links = [...text.matchAll(/href=\"(\\/companyDetail\\/(\\d{10}))\"/g)].map(m => m[2]);\n    return [...new Set(links)];\n  } catch (e) {\n    return [];\n  }\n}\n\nasync function run() {\n  console.log(`Searching MarketBZ for all 77 targets...`);\n  const foundInMbz = [];\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < targets.length; i++) {\n    const t = targets[i];\n    const cClean = cleanName(t.name);\n    const links = await searchMarketbz(cClean);\n    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 120));\n\n    // For each link, check if it's Busan\n    let matched = null;\n    for (const bz of links) {\n      if (bz === '2052172706') continue; // MarketBZ's own number in footer\n      const dUrl = `https://marketbz.com/companyDetail/${bz}`;\n      const dRes = await fetch(dUrl, { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0' } });\n      const dText = await dRes.text();\n      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100));\n\n      const desc = dText.match(/meta\\s+name=\"description\"\\s+content=\"([^\"]+)\"/)?.[1] || '';\n      if (desc.includes('부산')) {\n        const formatted = bz.replace(/(\\d{3})(\\d{2})(\\d{5})/, '$1-$2-$3');\n        console.log(`[MBZ FOUND] ${t.seq} ${t.name} -> ${formatted} | ${desc}`);\n        matched = { seq: t.seq, name: t.name, bz: formatted, desc };\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (matched) foundInMbz.push(matched);\n  }\n\n  console.log(`MarketBZ scan finished: found ${foundInMbz.length}`);\n  fs.writeFileSync('mbz_scan_results.json', JSON.stringify(foundInMbz, null, 2), 'utf8');\n}\n\nrun();\n","Description":"Scan MarketBZ for all targets","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\worktrees\\resilient-bardeen\\parse_company_data\\scan_mbz_all.js","toolAction":"Writing scan_mbz script","toolSummary":"Write scan_mbz_all.js"}}]}
